  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 224 PM MDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nFor Friday and into the weekend, warmer and drier air within more westerly \nflow works back into the region, as upper level ridging builds back across the \nGreat Basin and into the Rockies. This leads to warming and drying trend \nareawide through the weekend. With the drier air moving into the area, will \nneed to watch for possible freezing overnight temperatures, especially across\nthe high mountain valleys. By early next week, latest models indicate the \nupper ridge flattening across the region, allowing for occasional disturbances\nwithin the stronger flow in place across the Northern Tier, to bring occasional\nchances for precipitation and slightly cooler temperatures into the middle of \nnext week.",
